A||||4||DecadenceR||Removing Sail Panels||||1||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||06-22-2001||12:15 AM||||I want to take the entire sail panel off of my 84. What's the easiest way to get them out? Thanks!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||06-22-2001||12:21 AM||||Remove inside sail panel. <BR>Remove nut.<BR>gently pry 2 remaining clips from trailing edge where they insert into body.<BR>If replacing with new unit. remove nut rip off body.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steven||06-22-2001||09:57 AM||||You might want to look here: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||06-22-2001||10:14 AM||||You need to use the bolt removal method for the 84 glass sail panels. They will not pry off. Only the 85 thru 88 will.||||reg||4
Z||000004||DecadenceR||06-22-2001||12:04 PM||||Thanks guys.<BR>And no, I'm not replacing them, just starting to strip the 84 for anything I may have that's neede dor useful since I'm getting rid of it this week.||||reg||1
